### 1. Get JWT token for USER -> 200
POST http://localhost:8080/api/v1/auth/authenticate
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "user@books.com",
  "password": "user"
}

### 2. Get JWT token for ADMIN -> 200
POST http://localhost:8080/api/v1/auth/authenticate
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "admin@books.com",
  "password": "admin"
}

### 3. Get JWT token for SUPERADMIN -> 200
POST http://localhost:8080/api/v1/auth/authenticate
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "superadmin@books.com",
  "password": "superadmin"
}

### 4. Wrong password -> 401, no token
POST http://localhost:8080/api/v1/auth/authenticate
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "user@books.com",
  "password": "wrong"
}

###
